  "facts": [
    "The 1939 Kosciuszko Bridge, a six‑lane truss structure, opened on August 23, 1939, and was renamed in 1940 after Polish general Tadeusz Kościuszko during a ceremony attended by 15,000 people.",
    "In 2017, the first of two cable‑stayed spans opened, carrying five lanes eastbound, while the original truss bridge was demolished by controlled explosion in October 2017.",
    "The new westbound cable‑stayed span, completed August 29, 2019, added a bike and pedestrian path, expanding the crossing to six lanes total and a dedicated non‑motorized corridor."
